/* The three sentences iOS shows before it hands over a permission, in English.

   These are not decoration. The microphone one is the only moment the system
   gives this app to say, before the first recording, that the audio leaves the
   phone — and until 16 Aug 2026 it never said so anywhere. A translation that
   dropped that clause would be a worse lie in English than the Finnish ever
   was, so it is the clause the English keeps hardest.

   The Finnish originals live in ios/project.yml, which generates Info.plist. */

"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "Kinlore records the memories you tell in your own voice, so that your family can listen to them later. In a family archive the voice is sent through the OpenRouter service to an AI that writes the speech down as text. It is not used to train AI. In the archive the recording is stored encrypted.";

"NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription" = "Choose old photographs for your family to tell memories about.";

"NSCameraUsageDescription" = "Kinlore photographs old pictures to keep, so that your family can tell their memories of them.";
